# The crash and restart matrix (RD-140-04, axis A): which crates' `failpoints` feature it turns on
# and what it runs. Read by scripts/lib/crash-matrix.sh for scripts/check.sh and the
# `crash-matrix` job of .github/workflows/ci.yml; AGENTS.md points here (RD-191-09: the list was
# kept by hand in four places).
#
#     <package> [<nextest selection>]
#
# Every package without a selection joins one shared run: `--features <package>/failpoints` and
# `-p <package>` for each, filtered to the tests the feature turns on — a test behind it carries
# `crash` in its binary, module or name (RD-1120-08; scripts/tests/crash-matrix.sh holds that). A package with a selection runs alone, its own feature on, with that
# selection. The feature is off everywhere else, so the shipped build has no crash point in it, and
# each crash-test file is gated on the feature of the crate that owns its point — rd-core's alone
# turns none of the others on, and a binary compiled to nothing reports success.
#
# A new persistence path gets its point in rd_crash_points::CRASH_POINTS, its row in
# crates/rd-core/recovery-matrix.md, a case — and, in a crate not listed yet, its line here.
rd-core
rd-http
rd-scheduler
rd-usenet
rd-object-storage
rd-backup
rd-plugin-host
rd-extract
rd-api-core
rd-torrent
rd-plugin-transfer
rd-transfer-file
rd-update
# The plugin update's two points sit in rd-api-admin and are driven through the admin suite, so
# only those cases of rd-api run (RD-180-12).
rd-api      --test admin stopped_updates
# The vault's three points (archive passwords, the sweep at start) sit in rd-db; their binary
# alone (RD-190-04, RD-191-04), and the download history's point beside it (RD-1100-04).
rd-db       --test archive_password_crash --test download_history_crash
